0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 72 720 Td (Dara Whitfield) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 72 696 Td (Year 10 English, Ms Haddad, Period 3) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 72 672 Td (11 November 2026) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F4 16 Tf 108 624 Td (Give Us the Quiet Back) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 108 576 Td (The loudest sound at my old primary school was laughter. The loudest sound at Fairmount, at) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 72 552 Td (lunch, is the buzzing of phones on the tables. I do not want to sound old, because I am) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 72 528 Td (fifteen and I like my phone as much as anyone. But I think the school day would be better if) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 72 504 Td (we gave the phones a break, and I want to explain why.) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 108 480 Td (Let me begin with the numbers. A study of English schools by the London School of Economics) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 72 456 Td (found that banning phones raised results by about as much as adding five days to the school) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 72 432 Td (year, and that it helped the weakest students most. If the school could buy that much) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 72 408 Td (learning for free, we would be silly to say no. The cost is that for a few hours a day, we) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 72 384 Td (are a little less connected.) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 108 360 Td (Then there is what the numbers cannot show. In my netball team, we used to talk on the bus) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 72 336 Td (to the game. Now half the team listens to music and the other half watches videos. I am not) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 72 312 Td (saying anybody is wrong, but we have lost something small and warm. A day with no phones) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 72 288 Td (would give some of it back.) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 108 264 Td (The usual objection is that students need to reach their parents. I agree that there must be) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 72 240 Td (a way, and there is one: the front office. Parents can call, and the office can find us in) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 72 216 Td (two minutes. In an emergency that is faster and safer than a thousand text messages.) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 72 192 Td (Students who need a phone for medical reasons should be able to keep one, and the rule) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 72 168 Td (should say so.) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 108 144 Td (In summary, a locker rule is fair, it is simple and it works. It supports learning, it helps) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 72 120 Td (friendships and it protects the students who find it hardest to look away. I would ask the) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 72 96 Td (school to try it for one term and see what it sounds like. I think it will sound like) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 12 Tf 72 72 Td (laughter.) Tj ET
0.102 0.102 0.102 rg BT /F3 11 Tf 470 752 Td (Whitfield 1) Tj ET
